{%- comment -%}
  Promo banner overlaid on a product's main (featured) image.

  Shows only when the product metafield custom.image_offer_badge has a value,
  e.g. "FREE $50 Gift Certificate with purchase". Clear the metafield in
  Shopify admin (Products > [product] > Metafields > Image offer badge) to
  remove the banner — no theme edit needed.

  Rendered from snippets/media.liquid for the product's featured (main)
  image only, so it shows on the product page and quick view. It's a CSS
  overlay, not part of the image file, so the product image sent to Google
  Shopping stays clean (Google disapproves promo overlays).

  Pass in:
  * prod: product (avoid collision with global product)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign offer_badge_text = prod.metafields.custom.image_offer_badge.value -%}

{%- if offer_badge_text != blank -%}
  <style>
    .media:has(> .abz-offer-badge) {
      position: relative;
    }
    .abz-offer-badge {
      position: absolute;
      top: 12px;
      left: 12px;
      z-index: 2;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.5em;
      max-width: calc(100% - 24px);
      padding: 0.55em 1em;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: #e51515;
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: clamp(12px, 1.6vw, 16px);
      line-height: 1.2;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
      pointer-events: none; /* let clicks through to the lightbox/zoom */
    }
    .abz-offer-badge__icon {
      flex: none;
      font-size: 1.2em;
      line-height: 1;
    }
  </style>
  <div class="abz-offer-badge">
    <span class="abz-offer-badge__icon" aria-hidden="true">🎁</span>
    <span class="abz-offer-badge__text">{{ offer_badge_text | escape }}</span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
